# PP275: scripts/chiaki-ng.iss used to be ignored here, and it arrived with the file.
# Upstream generated the Inno Setup script from a wizard, so ignoring its output was
# right there. This port edits it by hand instead, which makes it source. The rule was
# inert only because git honours it for untracked paths and the file is tracked - the
# move it breaks is deleting and restoring it, where `git add` declines without a word.
#
# scripts/Output stays: that one really is ISCC's default output directory, and a
# hand-run compile that passes no OutputDir still lands there.
scripts/Output
.vs
CMakeSettings.json
chiaki.rb
gui/chiaking.rc
*.jks
secret.tar
keystore-env.sh
compile_commands.json
.ccls-cache
.cache/
.gdb_history
chiaki.conf
/appimage
.cache/
*.vscode
site/

# roadkeep's own working directory: lint reports and run state, regenerated on
# demand and never read by another clone.
.roadkeep/

# Claude Code's project directory is local state except for the files roadkeep
# needs a clone to carry: settings.json declares the marketplace and enables the
# plugin, hooks/ holds the launcher that gives Claude Code on the web (which has
# no `/plugin`) the same guard a local machine gets from the plugin, and skills/
# is the copy `roadkeep install` keeps in step.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/hooks/
!/.claude/skills/
